          "text": "{\"regions\":{\"r2\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Another account of the descent of the Ganges, however, states\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"that Jahnu was a Rishi performing penance and that the Gan-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"ges in its course having disturbed the sage in his concentration\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"by flooding the country where he was, the sage in anger stopp-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"ed the course of the river by pressing it under his thigh. At\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"Bh\u00e2giratha\u2019s earnest entreaties, however, he let the stream flow\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"again. \u0915\u0928\u094d\u0926\u0930 and \u0926\u0930\u0940 are usually given as synonymous terms;\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"( \u0926\u0930\u0940 \u0924\u0941 \u0915\u0928\u094d\u0926\u0930\u094b \u0935\u093e \u0938\u094d\u0924\u094d\u0930\u0940 Amara; while \u0915\u0941\u091e\u094d\u091c has a different shade of\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"meaning. \u0928\u093f\u0915\u0941\u091e\u094d\u091c\u0915\u0941\u091e\u094d\u091c\u094c \u0935\u093e \u0915\u094d\u0932\u0940\u092c\u0947 \u0932\u0924\u093e\u0926\u093f\u092a\u093f\u0939\u093f\u0924\u094b\u0926\u0930\u0947 Amara. A \u0915\u0941\u091e\u094d\u091c is a\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":10,\"text\":\"hollow in a mountain covered over with creepers and other\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":11,\"text\":\"plants. \u0926\u0930\u0940 is a cave, a hollow dug out or opened up in the side\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":12,\"text\":\"of a hill; and \u0915\u0928\u094d\u0926\u0930, though synonymous with \u0926\u0930\u0940 should rather\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":13,\"text\":\"be taken here to mean the gorge or defile between two hills, in\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":14,\"text\":\"which sense it is used in sl. 26. \u0915\u094d\u0935\u091a\u093f\u0924\u094d\u2014somewhere. For \u0926\u0930\u0940 read\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":15,\"text\":\"\u0924\u091f\u0940 in the text.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Some of the Sanskrit quotation is difficult to distinguish in the scan.\"},\"r3\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 80. \u0930\u092e\u094d\u092f\u0902 \u0938\u093e\u0927\u0941 &c.\u2014company of religious people can not\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"but be pleasing. \u0924\u0930\u0932\u092e\u094d\u2013glistening, beaming; cf. \u0928 \u092a\u094d\u0930\u092d\u093e\u0924\u0930\u0932\u0902 \u091c\u094d\u092f\u094b\u0924\u093f-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"\u0930\u0941\u0926\u0947\u0924\u093f \u0935\u0938\u0941\u0927\u093e\u0924\u0932\u093e\u0924\u094d S\u2019ak. R\u00e2marshi gives \u091a\u092a\u0932\u092e\u094d as its explanation.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"\u0909\u092a\u093e\u0939\u093f\u0924\u2014placed ( there, by anger. ). \u0905\u0928\u093f\u0924\u094d\u092f\u0924\u093e\u092e\u0941\u092a\u0917\u0924\u0947 &c.\u2014When\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"the mind has become unsteady, i. e. is not in its usual mood,\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"nothing pleases it. Or when the thoughts of the mutability of\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"this existence cross the mind, it becomes distracted and then\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":10,\"text\":\"it cannot relish anything earthly, except the joy of Brahman.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"The Sanskrit quotation and some quoted words are indistinct.\"},\"r4\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 81. \u092a\u094d\u0930\u0940\u0924\u092f\u0947\u2014the dat. case as indicating the result. \u0926\u0940\u092a\u093e\u0919\u094d\u0915\u0941\u0930-\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"the tapering, flame. \u091b\u093e\u092f\u093e\u2014shadow. R\u00e2marshi explains it by\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"\u0906\u0924\u092a\u092a\u094d\u0930\u0924\u094d\u092f\u0928\u0940\u0915\u093e\u2014( the contrary of light ) which Mr. Telang does\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"not accept. He gives it the meaning of \u2018flame\u2019; but as the\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"word \u0926\u0940\u092a\u093e\u0919\u094d\u0915\u0941\u0930 already occurs the word \u091b\u093e\u092f\u093e would be redundant\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"if it were taken to signify \u2018flame.\u2019 The shadow thrown by the\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"flickering flame of a lamp is even more unsteady than the flame\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"on account of its magnitude. \u0906\u0915\u0932\u092f\u094d\u092f\u2014having fully compre-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"hended or known.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"The Sanskrit word on line 3 is not entirely clear.\"},\"r5\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 82. \u0906\u0938\u0902\u0938\u093e\u0930\u0902-\u0924\u094d\u0930\u093f\u092d\u0941\u0935\u0928\u092e\u094d &c.\u2014( Searching through ) the\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"three worlds where the course of worldly life prevails:\u2014Telang,\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"\u2018The mind is deeply attached to sensual objects as the elephant\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null},\"r1\":{\"type\":\"page_number\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"( 73 )\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null}},\"units\":[{\"id\":\"u1\",\"type\":\"notes\",\"number\":null,\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"u2\",\"u3\",\"u4\",\"u5\"]},{\"id\":\"u2\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":null,\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r2\"]},{\"id\":\"u3\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"80\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r3\"]},{\"id\":\"u4\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"81\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r4\"]},{\"id\":\"u5\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"82\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"r5\"]}],\"flows\":[{\"flow\":\"main\",\"units\":[\"u1\"]}],\"relations\":[]}"
